! mcp_bootstrap_p350.strap -- MCP printed page 350: the $DUMP program's
! hex/mnemonic tail of the octal-hex line (ADHEX/AOCTLJ loops), the
! mnemonics switch ADHMN (NOP/B over ADOHND), the line writer AWRITE
! ($MCP B,DMCP with ,DSPR / ,APCOL1($11) / ,1.), the word compare
! AWDCMP (count equal words over the dump range, ACMPB), and the
! "ALL CONTAIN" print setup through ALCRFB/ALCRF, lines 1-50.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_250-445.pdf PDF p.100, read at 400 dpi, names at 900
! dpi.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 22$DUMP  CARD ID
! VB000352  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 350"; the heading row's
! LOCATION field is 235315, line 1's word.
!
! >>> A DIFFERENT PROGRAM AT OVERLAPPING ADDRESSES. <<<  PUNID 22$DUMP,
! card IDs VB...: still the $DUMP overlay assembled over the LOADER's
! area (both SLC,YMPBUF); no LOADER symbol is used here.
!
! THE PAGE.  50 lines; every line number prints a "*".  "*" after the
! LOCATION on lines 13, 32, 50.  No remark cards, no remarks.  Located
! rows contiguous from 235315.00 (line 1) to 235353.00 (line 50, SF, a
! full word; next 235354.00), then blank paper.  No TAIL.
!
! JOIN.  p.345 ends at 235103.40 (VB000168); pp.346-349 are in
! parallel transcription.  Line 1 is 235315.00; the next page should
! open at 235354.00.
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * line 10's label prints "ACCHND" / "ADCHND" (second glyph a D with
!     its stem, third an OPEN round); line 7's NOP operand prints
!     "ADOHND" with a CLOSED O at 900 dpi.  NOP,X prints X+.30 (line 7
!     235322.30 against line 10's 235322.00), so the two are the same
!     symbol; the closed glyph decides: written ADOHND in both places.
!   * "ACMPND" (lines 10, 35) and "ADMPND" (line 37): the D prints with
!     a worn stem; landed decks (pp.342-344) spell ADMPND.  Written
!     ADMPND.
!   * AOCTLJ (line 4), AOCTHB (line 12): the O prints closed at 900 dpi
!     and the family is AOCT- (pp.327-328, 344-345).
!   * ADHMN, ACTLBT, ACMPB: spelled as C22-6728 prints them (the $DUMP
!     indicator list, OCR text line ~36925: "ADHMN.19", "ACTLBT", "used by ACMPB").
!   * octal / hex fields with an open round read 0 ("FO" = F0, ".CC" =
!     .00).  Line 28's BZXE byte prints "CO": BZXE,$+1. assembles C0
!     (a real C, the branch-on-index op byte), so kept C0.
!
! EXTERNALS.  APUML6 is defined by landed p.342 (B,$ label, half word);
! DMCP, DSPR are landed (p.105/108); the others are defined on pages
! not yet landed; values from this page's binary (each comment says
! how much it fixes) or copied from the landed $DUMP stand-ins
! (pp.342-345).
!
! CARD SERIALS.  VB000352 .. VB000397.  Shared serials, every one a
! SIC/B pair: lines 5-6 (356), 31-32 (381), 39-40 (388), 47-48 (395).
! None skipped.

ADHEX   SYN, (8)235312.40            ! not landed; CB,$14 line 2 235312.74, half word only
AOCTLJ  SYN, (8)235306.0             ! not landed; CB,$13 line 4 235306.32, half word only
AMNEM0  SYN, (8)235402.0             ! p.351 line 30 defines it (AMNEM0, the first of AMNEM0/AMNEM1); BXE line 9 235402.32, half word only
ADMPND  SYN, (8)236162.0             ! not landed; KV line 10 236162.32, KV line 35 / LV line 37 236162.04, half word only
AOCTHB  SYN, (8)235301.0             ! not landed; BXL line 12 235301.32, half word only
ACTLBT  SYN, (8)236147.06            ! not landed; CM0000 line 13 236147.06, BIT-EXACT
